Print a tree of documentation paths

Builds a directory-like tree from all page paths stored in the documentation database.

Examples:
  docs_tree
  docs_tree {"depth": 2}
  docs_tree {"filter": "sdk"}

The tree prints as one JSON object, {"children": [node, ...]}. Each node has name, the last segment of its path, and path. A node has title when it is a page, and then `docs_show` accepts its path. A node has children, sorted by name, when it has child nodes that `depth` did not remove. When no page matches, the output is {"children": []}.
